    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aafca0f1_2863ca61",
        "filename": "drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-05T10:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why?  Is there a lock that should be used somewhere else instead?",
      "parentUuid": "5ff6ed44_fe94711c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1116,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "65512cf8a0825f45acbcd65b6865834ca41fb6d2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de0cb4f7_40296478",
        "filename": "drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-05T15:44:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, there is the `epfile-\u003effs-\u003eeps_lock` spinlock which this is technically protected by. However, that spinlock is meant to protect the ep from being torn down during an active transfer, and there\u0027s concern that the dynamic nature of this flag could cause issue with the io thread that is active. So more of a static vs dynamic locking concern. \n\nThere is also the `ffs-\u003emutex`, but we don\u0027t want to introduce this on the io thread as that could serialize things too much, and open up deadlock situations when contending for that and the eps_lock spinlock.\n\nTherefore, under the existing spinlock, the main concern is that the compiler would optimize or cache this value in some way. \n\nTherefore the proposal is to wrap these reads and writes with READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE, which prevents the compiler from caching this value. Another option is to change the definition from `u8` to `unsigned long` and use atomic bitops on it, though that will use more memory, and is slightly unnecessary for a single flag/bit.\n\nDo you have a preference?",
      "parentUuid": "aafca0f1_2863ca61",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1116,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "65512cf8a0825f45acbcd65b6865834ca41fb6d2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe746855_cd61fda6",
        "filename": "drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_fs.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-05T19:00:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about this further, the spinlock should be a memory barrier, and there are exactly one read/write operation within the critical section, so this is a non issue. \n\nResolving as we are protected by the `eps_lock`. Please feel free to re-open if I\u0027m wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "de0cb4f7_40296478",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1116,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "65512cf8a0825f45acbcd65b6865834ca41fb6d2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
